    <div role="tabpanel" id="svc-panel-keys" aria-labelledby="svc-tab-keys" tabindex="0" hidden>
      <p class="muted">Keys are saved to <code>.env</code> on this computer. They are never shown again, and never sent to your browser or to GitHub. Type a new key to replace one, or remove it.</p>
      <h3 class="svc-sub">Search services</h3>
      <div id="settings-search" class="settings-rows"></div>
      <h3 class="svc-sub">Free job APIs (real postings in Germany)</h3>
      <p class="muted">The search asks these for internships in Germany. Each is free; without its key it is skipped. Saved keys apply to the next search.</p>
      <details class="settings-how">
        <summary>How to get each key</summary>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Adzuna</strong> (250 searches a day): <a href="https://developer.adzuna.com/signup" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">sign up</a>, create an application, then copy its <em>app ID</em> and <em>app key</em> into the two Adzuna rows.</li>
          <li><strong>Jooble</strong> (500 requests per key, ever): <a href="https://de.jooble.org/api/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">fill the request form on the Germany site</a>. The key arrives by e-mail. A key from jooble.org covers US listings only. A search uses about 6 requests, so search when you need to.</li>
          <li><strong>Careerjet</strong>: <a href="https://www.careerjet.com/partners/api/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">open a publisher account</a> and copy the key from its API page. Then fill <em>Your IP address</em> with your public IP (search "what is my IP"); Careerjet refuses searches without it.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="muted">Adzuna, Jooble and Careerjet answer with their own listings; nothing is read from other sites.</p>
      </details>
      <div id="settings-jobapis" class="settings-rows"></div>
      <h3 class="svc-sub">Connectors (MCP, no key)</h3>
      <p class="muted">These come through your Claude account, so there is nothing to paste here. Connect them in Claude under Settings, Connectors.</p>
      <div class="settings-rows">
        <div class="settings-row"><label>Indeed</label><span>Connected through Claude. Searched by the workspace search.</span></div>
        <div class="settings-row"><label>Apify</label><span>Connected through Claude. Searched by the workspace search for StepStone and Arbeitsagentur, through community Actors billed per result on your Apify account. Private tracker only.</span></div>
        <div class="settings-row"><label>NVIDIA NIM</label><span>Searches LinkedIn and other boards through search APIs (Tavily, Exa, Firecrawl, Arbeitnow) with an NVIDIA model, so Claude spends no tokens there. Needs <code>NVIDIA_API_KEY</code> in <code>.env</code>. Search leads only, never opened. Private tracker only.</span></div>
      </div>
      <h3 class="svc-sub">Email sending (applications by email)</h3>
      <div id="settings-email" class="settings-rows"></div>
      <h3 class="svc-sub">Other API keys</h3>
      <div id="settings-custom" class="settings-rows"></div>
      <div class="settings-add">
        <input id="custom-name" type="text" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Name, e.g. SERPER_API_KEY" aria-label="Name of the new key">
        <input id="custom-value" type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Paste the key" aria-label="Value of the new key">
        <button type="button" class="btn" id="custom-add"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> Add key</button>
      </div>
      <small class="settings-help">A name must end in <code>_API_KEY</code>, <code>_KEY</code>, <code>_TOKEN</code> or <code>_SECRET</code>. Tools and MCP servers that read <code>${NAME}</code> pick it up.</small>
    </div>

    <div role="tabpanel" id="svc-panel-ai" aria-labelledby="svc-tab-ai" tabindex="0" hidden>
      <p class="muted">Used for suggestions, job scoring and CV/letter tailoring. Pick one provider and add its key.</p>
      <div id="settings-ai" class="settings-rows"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <footer class="svc-foot">
